From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucas gelfond <lucasgelfond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] demux: flac: seek over large metadata blocks

Metadata blocks the demuxer does not parse were skipped with a NULL read,
which the stream core serves 256 bytes at a time. The FLAC test suite has
files with 16 MiB PADDING and APPLICATION blocks: skipping them took
seconds before the first sample. Seek over the block instead, and only
fall back to reading when the stream cannot seek.
---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/flac.c b/modules/demux/flac.c
--- a/modules/demux/flac.c
+++ b/modules/demux/flac.c
@@ -755,7 +755,11 @@ static int  ParseHeaders( demux_t *p_demux, es_format_t *p_fmt )
                 ParsePicture( p_demux, p_peek, i_peek );
         }
 
-        if( vlc_stream_Read( p_demux->s, NULL, 4+i_len ) != (4+i_len) )
+        /* Seek over the block: PADDING or APPLICATION blocks can be
+         * megabytes, and skipping by reading goes 256 bytes at a time */
+        uint64_t i_next = vlc_stream_Tell( p_demux->s ) + 4 + i_len;
+        if( vlc_stream_Seek( p_demux->s, i_next ) != VLC_SUCCESS &&
+            vlc_stream_Read( p_demux->s, NULL, 4+i_len ) != (4+i_len) )
             break;
     }
 
